<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niccolò Gattilusio (lord of Lesbos)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1462">1462</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Niccolò <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gattilusio">Gattilusio</a> was the last Genoese lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesbos">Lesbos</a>, who seized power by murdering his brother Domenico in 1458. A tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, he could not resist when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-ii">Mehmed II</a> besieged Mytilene in 1462. After the surrender he was taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, where he converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> but was soon executed.</p></div>
